NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000271 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000272 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000273 "Test::Fatal - incredibly simple helpers for testing code with exceptions"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000274 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000275 "=head1 VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000276 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000277 "version 0.018"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000278 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000279 "=head1 SYNOPSIS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000280 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000281 "  use Test::More;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000282 "  use Test::Fatal;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000283 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000284 "  use System::Under::Test qw(might_die);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000285 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000286 "  is("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000287 "    exception { might_die; },"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000288 "    undef,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000289 "    \"the code lived\","
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000290 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000291 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000292 "  like("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000293 "    exception { might_die; },"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000294 "    qr/turns out it died/,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000295 "    \"the code died as expected\","
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000296 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000297 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000298 "  isa_ok("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000299 "    exception { might_die; },"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000300 "    'Exception::Whatever',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000301 "    'the thrown exception',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000302 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000303 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000304 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000305 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000306 "Test::Fatal is an alternative to the popular L<Test::Exception>.  It does much"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000307 "less, but should allow greater flexibility in testing exception-throwing code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000308 "with about the same amount of typing."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000309 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000310 "It exports one routine by default: C<exception>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000311 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000312 "B<Achtung!>  C<exception> intentionally does not manipulate the call stack."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000313 "User-written test functions that use C<exception> must be careful to avoid"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000314 "false positives if exceptions use stack traces that show arguments.  For a more"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000315 "magical approach involving globally overriding C<caller>, see"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000316 "L<Test::Exception>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000317 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000318 "=head1 PERL VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000319 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000320 "This library should run on perls released even a long time ago.  It should"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000321 "work on any version of perl released in the last five years."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000322 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000323 "Although it may work on older versions of perl, no guarantee is made that the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000324 "minimum required version will not be increased.  The version may be increased"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000325 "for any reason, and there is no promise that patches will be accepted to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000326 "lower the minimum required perl."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000327 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000328 "=head1 FUNCTIONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000329 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000330 "=head2 exception"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000331 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000332 "  my $exception = exception { ... };"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000333 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000334 "C<exception> takes a bare block of code and returns the exception thrown by"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000335 "that block.  If no exception was thrown, it returns undef."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000336 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000337 "B<Achtung!>  If the block results in an I<unblessed false> exception, such as 0"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000338 "or the empty string, Test::Fatal itself will die.  Since either of these cases"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000339 "indicates a serious problem with the system under testing, this behavior is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000340 "considered a I<feature>. Note that this issue is only known to occur on perls"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000341 "before 5.14."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000342 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000343 "Exercise caution if you must test for these conditions: wrapping C<exception {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000344 "... }> in an C<ok()> block will not give you the result you need, so make sure"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000345 "you use C<is()> instead.  You can also directly use L<Try::Tiny>'s try/catch"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000346 "mechanism, the underlying exception handling system of Test::Fatal."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000347 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000348 "Note that there is no TAP assert being performed.  In other words, no \"ok\" or"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000349 "\"not ok\" line is emitted.  It's up to you to use the rest of C<exception> in an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000350 "existing test like C<ok>, C<isa_ok>, C<is>, et cetera.  Or you may wish to use"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000351 "the C<dies_ok> and C<lives_ok> wrappers, which do provide TAP output."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000352 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000353 "C<exception> does I<not> alter the stack presented to the called block, meaning"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000354 "that if the exception returned has a stack trace, it will include some frames"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000355 "between the code calling C<exception> and the thing throwing the exception."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000356 "This is considered a I<feature> because it avoids the occasionally twitchy"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000357 "C<Sub::Uplevel> mechanism."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000358 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000359 "B<Achtung!>  This is not a great idea:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000360 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000361 "  sub exception_like(&$;$) {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000362 "      my ($code, $pattern, $name) = @_;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000363 "      like( &exception($code), $pattern, $name );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000364 "  }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000365 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000366 "  exception_like(sub { }, qr/foo/, 'foo appears in the exception');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000367 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000368 "If the code in the C<...> is going to throw a stack trace with the arguments to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000369 "each subroutine in its call stack (for example via C<Carp::confess>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000370 "the test name, \"foo appears in the exception\" will itself be matched by the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000371 "regex.  Instead, write this:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000372 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000373 "  like( exception { ... }, qr/foo/, 'foo appears in the exception' );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000374 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000375 "If you really want a test function that passes the test name, wrap the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000376 "arguments in an array reference to hide the literal text from a stack trace:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000377 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000378 "  sub exception_like(&$) {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000379 "      my ($code, $args) = @_;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000380 "      my ($pattern, $name) = @$args;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000381 "      like( &exception($code), $pattern, $name );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000382 "  }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000383 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000384 "  exception_like(sub { }, [ qr/foo/, 'foo appears in the exception' ] );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000385 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000386 "To aid in avoiding the problem where the pattern is seen in the exception"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000387 "because of the call stack, C<$Carp::MaxArgNums> is locally set to -1 when the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000388 "code block is called.  If you really don't want that, set it back to whatever"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000389 "value you like at the beginning of the code block.  Obviously, this solution"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000390 "doens't affect all possible ways that args of subroutines in the call stack"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000391 "might taint the test.  The intention here is to prevent some false passes from"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000392 "people who didn't read the documentation.  Your punishment for reading it is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000393 "that you must consider whether to do anything about this."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000394 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000395 "B<Achtung>: One final bad idea:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000396 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000397 "  isnt( exception { ... }, undef, \"my code died!\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000398 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000399 "It's true that this tests that your code died, but you should really test that"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000400 "it died I<for the right reason>.  For example, if you make an unrelated mistake"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000401 "in the block, like using the wrong dereference, your test will pass even though"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000402 "the code to be tested isn't really run at all.  If you're expecting an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000403 "inspectable exception with an identifier or class, test that.  If you're"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000404 "expecting a string exception, consider using C<like>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000405 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000406 "=head2 success"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000407 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000408 "  try {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000409 "    should_live;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000410 "  } catch {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000411 "    fail(\"boo, we died\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000412 "  } success {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000413 "    pass(\"hooray, we lived\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000414 "  };"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000415 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000416 "C<success>, exported only by request, is a L<Try::Tiny> helper with semantics"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000417 "identical to L<C<finally>|Try::Tiny/finally>, but the body of the block will"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000418 "only be run if the C<try> block ran without error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000419 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000420 "Although almost any needed exception tests can be performed with C<exception>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000421 "success blocks may sometimes help organize complex testing."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000422 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000423 "=head2 dies_ok"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000424 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000425 "=head2 lives_ok"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000426 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000427 "Exported only by request, these two functions run a given block of code, and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000428 "provide TAP output indicating if it did, or did not throw an exception."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000429 "These provide an easy upgrade path for replacing existing unit tests based on"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000430 "C<Test::Exception>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000431 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000432 "RJBS does not suggest using this except as a convenience while porting tests to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000433 "use Test::Fatal's C<exception> routine."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000434 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000435 "  use Test::More tests => 2;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000436 "  use Test::Fatal qw(dies_ok lives_ok);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000437 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000438 "  dies_ok { die \"I failed\" } 'code that fails';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000439 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000440 "  lives_ok { return \"I'm still alive\" } 'code that does not fail';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000441 ""
